From f9ec50b4b46ab0eb8c4b8281db159d694a3902e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:24:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] panvk/kbase: defer BO frees past open submissions;
 validation and fault tooling

- Keep BOs freed while a JM submission is open until every such submission
  has completed. kbase holds no reference on job memory, unlike the DRM
  drivers, so an early free became a GPU translation fault.
- PANVK_VALIDATE=1: track live BO ranges, check every address a Bifrost
  job's descriptors point at before submission, record frees with
  alloc/free backtraces, and write /proc/self/maps plus the free history
  next to the driver on the first failed submission.
- PANVK_FORCE_ROBUST=1: bounds-check all UBO/SSBO accesses.
- PANVK_KBASE_GROW_COMMIT_MB: initial commit of grow-on-fault heaps.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
